1
00:01:28,237 --> 00:01:34,076
ALLIGATOR THE ENTERTAINER

2
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,416
Only three yen left until payday.

3
00:01:41,651 --> 00:01:45,121
I can't afford a candy lucky dip, let alone a bet on the horses.

4
00:01:46,389 --> 00:01:47,256
What's this?

5
00:01:48,257 --> 00:01:49,759
A one-yen coin.

6
00:01:50,226 --> 00:01:53,062
Four yen's not much better than three...

7
00:01:53,262 --> 00:01:55,331
Hmm? Wait a minute.

8
00:01:57,199 --> 00:01:58,467
"GRAND REOPENING"

9
00:02:00,903 --> 00:02:03,973
Today is our grand reopening! No limit on payouts today!

10
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:07,610
-Go on, treat yourself! -Sir!

11
00:02:08,144 --> 00:02:10,446
It's that cop who won the big payout.

12
00:02:10,813 --> 00:02:12,748
Pull, and win! We hope you enjoy—

13
00:02:18,754 --> 00:02:19,655
We're in trouble!

14
00:02:23,092 --> 00:02:24,427
Whew, what a day!

15
00:02:24,627 --> 00:02:26,328
Now to close up for the day.

16
00:02:26,529 --> 00:02:28,764
Why close in the middle of the day?

17
00:02:29,799 --> 00:02:32,668
Well, a typhoon is coming, so we gotta close up shop.

18
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:35,171
Sorry, sir. Maybe next time.

19
00:02:35,805 --> 00:02:38,340
There's no typhoon coming! Huh?

20
00:02:39,942 --> 00:02:42,678
These two are former soccer and basketball athletes.

21
00:02:43,145 --> 00:02:44,513
They're pros at defense!

22
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:46,916
So that's how you wanna play?

23
00:02:47,316 --> 00:02:48,117
Outta my way!

24
00:02:54,857 --> 00:02:57,660
Looks pretty packed to me. Right, Mr. Manager?

25
00:02:58,627 --> 00:03:00,963
That was offside, sir!

26
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,133
One ball, please.

27
00:03:04,667 --> 00:03:06,869
We don't sell them individually.

28
00:03:07,636 --> 00:03:09,038
This is all I've got.

29
00:03:09,271 --> 00:03:10,372
Help a man out, yeah?

30
00:03:10,573 --> 00:03:11,373
But sir...

31
00:03:12,408 --> 00:03:14,110
You're being unreasonable here.

32
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:16,212
You can buy eggs one at a time!

33
00:03:16,879 --> 00:03:21,117
Even milk comes in 500 ml and 250 ml options these days.

34
00:03:21,317 --> 00:03:23,853
Pachinko parlors should adapt to consumer needs!

35
00:03:24,053 --> 00:03:25,054
But sir...

36
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:29,558
Surely he won't win big with just one pull?

37
00:03:29,758 --> 00:03:31,060
All right, fine.

38
00:03:32,328 --> 00:03:33,162
Very well.

39
00:03:33,362 --> 00:03:36,165
But you'll have to leave once you've made your shot.

40
00:03:36,365 --> 00:03:37,066
Of course.

41
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:40,503
No stealing floor balls either.

42
00:03:40,703 --> 00:03:41,403
Got it.

43
00:03:41,871 --> 00:03:43,139
Then it's agreed.

44
00:03:43,339 --> 00:03:46,442
You'll leave as soon as you've lost on the first go.

45
00:03:46,675 --> 00:03:48,777
I'm a man of my word.

46
00:03:49,011 --> 00:03:51,447
-All right. Give him his ball. -Okay.

47
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,414
Here.

48
00:03:52,615 --> 00:03:55,518
This is make or break. I spent all my money on you.

49
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:03,392
Now, which machine to choose?

50
00:04:08,364 --> 00:04:10,466
Oh no! That's a winning machine.

51
00:04:16,338 --> 00:04:18,707
Phew. He passed by the winning machine.

52
00:04:24,713 --> 00:04:27,349
Maybe I should go with this one after all.

53
00:04:28,284 --> 00:04:29,952
Oh no! My face gave it away!

54
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:31,453
Gotta stay calm.

55
00:04:36,392 --> 00:04:38,561
Hmm, maybe this other machine pays better.

56
00:04:42,932 --> 00:04:44,466
But this one is pulling me...

57
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:49,238
Ugh! One, two, three! One, two, three...

58
00:04:49,438 --> 00:04:50,806
This one?

59
00:04:51,407 --> 00:04:53,209
No, this one?

60
00:04:53,409 --> 00:04:55,211
Maybe that one?

61
00:04:55,611 --> 00:04:57,313
No, gotta be this one.

62
00:04:57,513 --> 00:04:59,048
Stop! I can't take it!

63
00:05:01,851 --> 00:05:05,054
A pachinko manager should have a better poker face.

64
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:08,991
Go!

65
00:05:15,965 --> 00:05:17,066
Yes!

66
00:05:18,767 --> 00:05:19,835
Come to papa!

67
00:05:25,507 --> 00:05:27,142
Heck yeah!

68
00:05:27,543 --> 00:05:29,011
Oh no!

69
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:31,313
Hide the good prizes! Quickly!

70
00:05:31,847 --> 00:05:35,117
He'll take everything! Hide it! Hurry!

71
00:05:36,518 --> 00:05:40,823
527,235 balls.

72
00:05:41,023 --> 00:05:44,260
First, I want five cases of juice, and ten boxes of biscuits.

73
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:48,297
Then, twenty cases each of canned BBQ meat, canned crab, and corned beef.

74
00:05:48,631 --> 00:05:51,267
A year's worth of toilet paper, and 100 pairs of undies.

75
00:05:51,467 --> 00:05:54,503
A sack of rice, and 18 liters each of miso, soy sauce, and sake.

76
00:05:54,703 --> 00:05:57,473
Throw in about 30 watches as well.

77
00:05:57,673 --> 00:06:00,542
I can pawn them to cover living expenses.

78
00:06:00,910 --> 00:06:04,213
Send it all over to Nikoniko Dormitory later.

79
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:06,548
How many balls are left?

80
00:06:06,749 --> 00:06:08,884
About 300,000 more.

81
00:06:09,685 --> 00:06:13,522
Please have mercy. You're bleeding us bone dry...

82
00:06:15,891 --> 00:06:17,693
Don't you have anything else?

83
00:06:19,695 --> 00:06:20,496
What are those?

84
00:06:20,696 --> 00:06:24,566
Well, I run a pet store on the side.

85
00:06:26,001 --> 00:06:31,006
I could give you any pet you like for the remaining 300,000?

86
00:06:32,007 --> 00:06:33,242
A pet, huh?

87
00:06:39,014 --> 00:06:41,050
Ryotsu is late again.

88
00:06:42,017 --> 00:06:45,688
He's already had a day off. Can't he show up on time the day after?

89
00:06:46,388 --> 00:06:48,490
Oh, here he is.

90
00:06:48,924 --> 00:06:52,061
Hey, Ryotsu. What time do you call this?

91
00:06:52,261 --> 00:06:54,063
Morning everyone.

92
00:06:57,499 --> 00:06:59,969
Ryotsu! What is that?

93
00:07:00,402 --> 00:07:02,805
What do you think? A surfboard?

94
00:07:03,038 --> 00:07:06,041
It's an alligator! Isn't he cute?

95
00:07:06,408 --> 00:07:08,510
It's pretty calm for an alligator.

96
00:07:08,711 --> 00:07:10,245
It's so still.

97
00:07:10,446 --> 00:07:13,549
Don't scare us like that, Ryotsu.

98
00:07:14,283 --> 00:07:16,251
What a well-made toy.

99
00:07:16,452 --> 00:07:17,586
Coochy-coochy-coo.

100
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:20,089
-Whoa! -It's real!

101
00:07:21,290 --> 00:07:24,793
He hasn't had his breakfast yet, so don't get too close.

102
00:07:24,994 --> 00:07:27,563
Y-You should have told me that first!

103
00:07:30,632 --> 00:07:32,801
Is that yummy meat, huh?

104
00:07:33,002 --> 00:07:35,304
Make sure you chew it well.

105
00:07:38,607 --> 00:07:41,643
He's a good boy, so long as I stay nearby and feed him.

106
00:07:42,444 --> 00:07:44,446
He won't be any trouble here.

107
00:07:44,813 --> 00:07:46,749
Oh, good boy, good boy.

108
00:07:46,949 --> 00:07:50,018
So cute. Snuggly-wuggly.

109
00:07:51,754 --> 00:07:55,858
Ryotsu, you're not seriously planning to keep that alligator, are you?

110
00:07:56,658 --> 00:07:59,328
Of course I am, Chief Ohara.

111
00:08:00,095 --> 00:08:04,867
It's been my dream to raise an alligator since I was a kid!

112
00:08:05,167 --> 00:08:07,302
I've never heard that before.

113
00:08:07,503 --> 00:08:09,838
Why not a dog or a cat? Why an alligator?

114
00:08:10,339 --> 00:08:15,844
Everyone misunderstands alligators. I can't help but relate to that.

115
00:08:16,512 --> 00:08:20,849
Look at his cute little eyes shining out from that scary-looking head.

116
00:08:21,517 --> 00:08:22,851
There's no need for that.

117
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:28,157
Stop it, Ryotsu! He'll bite!

118
00:08:28,357 --> 00:08:29,158
Ryo-chan!

119
00:08:29,525 --> 00:08:34,196
Their sharp teeth are only used for defense and to catch prey.

120
00:08:34,663 --> 00:08:37,499
They don't attack for no reason.

121
00:08:38,167 --> 00:08:39,501
Ryotsu!

122
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:47,609
Oh, he's just playing.

123
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:52,881
You cute little devil, you...

124
00:08:53,916 --> 00:08:57,052
Here's what you get. Mwah, mwah, mwah!

125
00:08:57,286 --> 00:08:58,987
Stop wriggling around!

126
00:09:00,022 --> 00:09:01,990
Mwah, mwah! Snuggly-wuggly!

127
00:09:02,691 --> 00:09:05,928
Come on, let's get you all squeaky clean.

128
00:09:06,328 --> 00:09:09,164
This will help your back to shine more.

129
00:09:11,667 --> 00:09:14,002
Don't be naughty.

130
00:09:14,636 --> 00:09:17,639
Come on, let's clean under your arms too.

131
00:09:20,209 --> 00:09:23,846
Ryo-chan is surprisingly good with animals, isn't he?

132
00:09:27,583 --> 00:09:30,953
After your bath, two careful coats of wax.

133
00:09:34,223 --> 00:09:36,258
What, are you hungry already?

134
00:09:36,792 --> 00:09:37,926
Of course you are.

135
00:09:38,594 --> 00:09:41,196
I suppose growing kids do have big appetites.

136
00:09:41,396 --> 00:09:44,766
All right, I'll feed you lots to become big and strong.

137
00:09:45,367 --> 00:09:48,770
There we go. Nice and clean.

138
00:09:49,204 --> 00:09:52,975
You keep pampering it like that and it'll never be a real alligator.

139
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:54,343
Who cares?

140
00:09:54,543 --> 00:09:58,247
As of this moment, I dedicate myself to alligator welfare.

141
00:09:58,447 --> 00:10:02,518
I'll fight for administrative reform on climate change and animal rights.

142
00:10:02,985 --> 00:10:04,520
Administrative reform?

143
00:10:05,254 --> 00:10:07,523
There's more to this, I think.

144
00:10:07,723 --> 00:10:08,457
Yeah.

145
00:10:10,792 --> 00:10:13,762
Eat lots, and grow nice and big and strong.

146
00:10:23,739 --> 00:10:25,240
Six, huh? Excellent.

147
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,141
An alligator?

148
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:28,243
You have good taste.

149
00:10:29,077 --> 00:10:33,749
A crocodile handbag such as this one sells for over 500,000 yen.

150
00:10:34,283 --> 00:10:37,019
Their leather is that pricey?

151
00:10:39,421 --> 00:10:41,190
You bet!

152
00:10:42,324 --> 00:10:46,962
You'll have a five-meter, four million yen alligator in five years' time.

153
00:10:47,930 --> 00:10:50,098
It's definitely a moneymaker.

154
00:10:57,105 --> 00:10:59,308
Four million yen in five years.

155
00:10:59,508 --> 00:11:00,642
So that's it.

156
00:11:00,842 --> 00:11:04,146
What are you all doing here?

157
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:07,149
What are you talking about, Nakagawa?

158
00:11:07,616 --> 00:11:12,421
You're raising that alligator for its skin to sell it for four million yen, right?

159
00:11:15,057 --> 00:11:16,124
I knew it.

160
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:18,961
Well, I don't want the leather to go hungry...

161
00:11:19,161 --> 00:11:21,863
No, I mean, the pachinko guy said...

162
00:11:22,364 --> 00:11:23,899
It's always money, isn't it?

163
00:11:24,132 --> 00:11:28,437
And to think I thought you'd turned a new leaf on animal welfare.

164
00:11:28,637 --> 00:11:32,975
What about people keeping chickens, cows, or pigs as pets, huh?

165
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:35,978
They sell those to make a living, right?

166
00:11:36,445 --> 00:11:37,479
Well, that's...

167
00:11:37,679 --> 00:11:40,315
So what's wrong with an alligator?

168
00:11:40,515 --> 00:11:43,218
I'm raising him as my own walking piggy ba— Huh?

169
00:11:43,819 --> 00:11:44,653
He's gone!

170
00:11:44,853 --> 00:11:47,222
-It went into the kitchen... -Ah!

171
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:48,490
What's wrong?

172
00:11:48,690 --> 00:11:49,858
Just look!

173
00:11:52,461 --> 00:11:54,930
It's standing on two legs.

174
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:57,499
Hey, that's...

175
00:11:57,699 --> 00:12:01,870
That's the meat I bought for our late-night snack! Don't eat that!

176
00:12:03,071 --> 00:12:04,573
Stop it, Reiko!

177
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:07,576
But it's eating all our meat!

178
00:12:07,809 --> 00:12:09,111
I'll pay you back.

179
00:12:09,578 --> 00:12:14,683
Just don't ever hurt my precious alligator again. Got it?

180
00:12:16,385 --> 00:12:17,653
It's mocking you.

181
00:12:17,853 --> 00:12:18,954
How dare you mock me!

182
00:12:19,488 --> 00:12:20,255
Ouch!

183
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:26,428
Now you need a walk?

184
00:12:26,928 --> 00:12:28,430
It's always about you, huh?

185
00:12:29,131 --> 00:12:31,566
Just where are you taking me?

186
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:33,368
Hey! Hey!

187
00:12:34,269 --> 00:12:35,837
Welcome.

188
00:12:36,138 --> 00:12:39,574
Yikes! This is that famous and expensive butcher shop.

189
00:12:41,143 --> 00:12:42,744
What would you like?

190
00:12:42,944 --> 00:12:45,080
No, I'm good today.

191
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:46,048
Ouch!

192
00:12:47,983 --> 00:12:49,518
Whoa! 4,000 yen per kilo?

193
00:12:50,085 --> 00:12:51,620
You can't be serious!

194
00:12:51,853 --> 00:12:53,955
Gimme three of those cheap, thick ones—

195
00:12:54,156 --> 00:12:54,956
Ouch!

196
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:01,897
He's gonna be turned into handbags worth four million yen.

197
00:13:02,097 --> 00:13:04,466
Maybe a little luxury now wouldn't hurt.

198
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,469
I'll have some of this fillet meat.

199
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:08,603
100 grams.

200
00:13:08,804 --> 00:13:09,638
Ouch!

201
00:13:12,808 --> 00:13:14,643
Make that a kilogram.

202
00:13:26,888 --> 00:13:29,024
Four thousand yen on fillet meat?

203
00:13:30,792 --> 00:13:33,028
Yeah, but he's like my own money tree.

204
00:13:33,562 --> 00:13:35,564
He's allowed to have his treats.

205
00:13:36,098 --> 00:13:39,334
You said four million yen in five years' time, right?

206
00:13:40,135 --> 00:13:44,573
Say, how much did you spend on meat for him today?

207
00:13:46,208 --> 00:13:50,579
I think the thigh meat was 2,940 yen for three kilos.

208
00:13:50,912 --> 00:13:52,814
So that's 7,000 yen total.

209
00:13:53,014 --> 00:13:54,850
What about your meat, Reiko-san?

210
00:13:55,050 --> 00:13:58,186
It was 1,000 yen worth of sirloin, at 200 yen per 100 grams.

211
00:13:59,988 --> 00:14:03,191
So just as an estimate, he's costing you 240,000 yen a month.

212
00:14:03,392 --> 00:14:04,025
What?

213
00:14:04,526 --> 00:14:06,328
That won't break even then.

214
00:14:07,996 --> 00:14:09,030
What was that?

215
00:14:09,231 --> 00:14:11,032
"DAILY FEED 8,000 YEN × 30 DAYS = 240,000 YEN"

216
00:14:14,302 --> 00:14:16,304
I want him to go for four million yen,

217
00:14:16,505 --> 00:14:21,042
so if I skip the fillet and keep costs down to 100,000 yen a month...

218
00:14:21,676 --> 00:14:23,512
That's 1.2 million yen a year,

219
00:14:23,712 --> 00:14:25,614
so six million yen in five years.

220
00:14:25,814 --> 00:14:29,084
Minus the cost of food leaves... minus two million yen?!

221
00:14:29,317 --> 00:14:30,051
Ryotsu...

222
00:14:30,719 --> 00:14:32,821
Never mind a profit!

223
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:35,390
I'll be in the red!

224
00:14:39,561 --> 00:14:41,963
I'M OUT OF MEAT

225
00:14:42,197 --> 00:14:43,331
Shut up!

226
00:14:43,532 --> 00:14:46,401
Damn that pachinko guy! He tricked me!

227
00:14:46,701 --> 00:14:49,104
Ryotsu, calm down.

228
00:14:49,337 --> 00:14:52,407
Let me go! He said this alligator would be a moneymaker!

229
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:56,178
He probably never calculated the cost of raising it.

230
00:14:56,378 --> 00:14:58,213
Damn it!

231
00:14:59,281 --> 00:15:01,383
The longer I keep him, the more I lose.

232
00:15:01,983 --> 00:15:03,385
That's too cruel!

233
00:15:03,585 --> 00:15:05,353
YOU'LL BE FINE

234
00:15:05,854 --> 00:15:08,089
I don't need your comfort!

235
00:15:10,058 --> 00:15:13,862
Now I know you're a money sink, I have no reason or funds to keep you.

236
00:15:15,096 --> 00:15:16,364
Get outta here! Scram!

237
00:15:16,932 --> 00:15:19,367
Go be a stray!

238
00:15:22,671 --> 00:15:25,440
STRAY ALLIGATOR

239
00:15:28,076 --> 00:15:30,579
It'll be you on the hook if he causes trouble.

240
00:15:30,779 --> 00:15:32,147
Why would I get fired?

241
00:15:32,848 --> 00:15:34,416
It'd be his own fault.

242
00:15:34,616 --> 00:15:35,917
He's your pet.

243
00:15:36,418 --> 00:15:40,121
Once he's in your care, he's your responsibility, Ryo-chan.

244
00:15:40,622 --> 00:15:42,224
All he does is eat and sleep.

245
00:15:42,424 --> 00:15:44,960
He's not even cute! He's no pet.

246
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,962
You good-for-nothing!

247
00:15:49,731 --> 00:15:52,100
That's a pretty flexible alligator.

248
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:56,037
Doing a bridge isn't going to bring in the dough.

249
00:15:56,504 --> 00:15:58,507
I've never seen anything like it.

250
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:00,642
I think it's really cute.

251
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:01,476
What?

252
00:16:05,513 --> 00:16:06,815
What else can you do?

253
00:16:16,458 --> 00:16:17,726
This might work.

254
00:16:17,926 --> 00:16:19,327
HEHE

255
00:16:19,527 --> 00:16:20,962
I WANT MEAT

256
00:16:21,596 --> 00:16:22,831
Not now!

257
00:16:23,498 --> 00:16:27,202
It's bird feed for you until you start bringing in the money.

258
00:16:31,973 --> 00:16:35,176
And this week's winning video is...

259
00:16:36,111 --> 00:16:39,080
The Clever Croc! The winner will receive 100,000 yen!

260
00:16:39,281 --> 00:16:40,549
Good job, Al!

261
00:16:41,349 --> 00:16:42,817
100,000 yen!

262
00:16:45,453 --> 00:16:46,688
All right, I got you.

263
00:16:46,922 --> 00:16:49,190
Starting tomorrow, you're getting dog food.

264
00:16:49,391 --> 00:16:51,326
DOG FOOD...

265
00:16:51,526 --> 00:16:55,096
This might even pay better than selling him off.

266
00:16:55,297 --> 00:16:57,198
"CLEVER CROC RIDES A BIKE!"

267
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:00,535
This Clever Croc showing off his bike skills

268
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:02,704
wins the prize of 100,000 yen.

269
00:17:07,108 --> 00:17:07,709
Al!

270
00:17:08,376 --> 00:17:11,212
You get real meat today for a change.

271
00:17:12,414 --> 00:17:14,849
But it's the cheap stuff. Chopped pork.

272
00:17:15,050 --> 00:17:15,984
WHAT?

273
00:17:16,184 --> 00:17:19,154
You want better meat? Win me some more money.

274
00:17:19,354 --> 00:17:21,656
You gotta earn your keep.

275
00:17:21,856 --> 00:17:22,490
Got it?

276
00:17:22,857 --> 00:17:24,993
I'LL DO IT

277
00:17:32,133 --> 00:17:36,504
Hey! Ten more serves of top sirloin and short ribs on the bone!

278
00:17:37,038 --> 00:17:38,673
Clever Croc wins again!

279
00:17:38,873 --> 00:17:41,009
That's four weeks in a row!

280
00:17:41,876 --> 00:17:42,577
Hey, sir!

281
00:17:43,144 --> 00:17:44,813
Gimme all these kits here.

282
00:17:45,914 --> 00:17:47,082
I've got the money.

283
00:17:53,355 --> 00:17:56,157
The cycling tricks are starting to get old.

284
00:17:57,859 --> 00:17:59,627
I DID IT! I DID IT!

285
00:18:00,195 --> 00:18:01,830
Think of something else.

286
00:18:04,432 --> 00:18:06,935
This sort of thing never gets old.

287
00:18:08,203 --> 00:18:10,238
You can't beat brilliance.

288
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:15,577
Yes, there it is! Give him a round of applause.

289
00:18:39,234 --> 00:18:43,405
Hey, Reiko. Still no calls from any TV stations?

290
00:18:43,605 --> 00:18:45,407
No, why?

291
00:18:45,607 --> 00:18:48,143
We've won all the amateur video shows,

292
00:18:48,576 --> 00:18:52,414
so I'm thinking it's about time the entertainment industry took notice.

293
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:54,149
Easier said than done.

294
00:18:54,349 --> 00:18:55,650
Hey! This is it!

295
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:57,919
Ah, that's the crocodile?

296
00:18:58,119 --> 00:18:59,454
Who are you guys?

297
00:19:00,221 --> 00:19:03,158
Yes, hello. I'm a producer from a TV station.

298
00:19:03,892 --> 00:19:07,462
We'd like for Clever Croc to appear on our show.

299
00:19:07,662 --> 00:19:10,932
Of course, we'll prepare plenty of meat for him.

300
00:19:14,302 --> 00:19:15,937
Oh, is that so?

301
00:19:16,371 --> 00:19:21,242
Well, I'm his manager, so I might just hear you out.

302
00:19:21,443 --> 00:19:23,344
And we'll work out the pay.

303
00:19:25,547 --> 00:19:26,848
What was that for?

304
00:19:29,851 --> 00:19:30,485
Huh?

305
00:19:30,685 --> 00:19:32,353
"You're the worst"?

306
00:19:35,924 --> 00:19:37,358
"You're fired"?!

307
00:19:37,559 --> 00:19:38,359
But why?

308
00:19:38,693 --> 00:19:42,831
You can't take 90% of someone's earnings, even if they are an alligator.

309
00:19:46,367 --> 00:19:48,269
He's gotten too big for his boots.

310
00:19:48,470 --> 00:19:53,575
But he's my priceless cash cow. I can't let him go now...

311
00:19:56,211 --> 00:20:01,182
Big Al! Please don't fire me! I'm begging you!

312
00:20:04,052 --> 00:20:08,223
This week's number one is the wildly popular Clever Croc!

313
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:14,896
You're so cool, Clever Croc!

314
00:20:15,997 --> 00:20:18,133
Here's a face from your past!

315
00:20:20,368 --> 00:20:24,172
I missed you! You've grown so much...

316
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:27,709
You lie through your teeth.

317
00:20:40,522 --> 00:20:42,323
Nice shot!

318
00:20:42,724 --> 00:20:48,163
Please come on our show next, Clever Croc!

319
00:20:50,031 --> 00:20:52,367
Look! He's so cute!

320
00:20:52,567 --> 00:20:57,105
Hey, isn't that Clever Croc? Wasn't he on the cover of CanCan?

321
00:20:57,338 --> 00:20:59,541
-He's really popular. -Yeah.

322
00:20:59,741 --> 00:21:05,046
Hey, you lot! Keep your noses out of this! Big Al is tired.

323
00:21:05,246 --> 00:21:06,748
Here's your coffee.

324
00:21:06,948 --> 00:21:09,751
Can you believe high school girls these days?

325
00:21:15,590 --> 00:21:20,228
I'm sorry, we only had instant. I'll make some fresh right away.

326
00:21:20,428 --> 00:21:21,462
Hmph.

327
00:21:23,565 --> 00:21:25,834
Damn it... You'll pay for this, Al!

328
00:21:26,401 --> 00:21:27,368
Hmm?

329
00:21:30,238 --> 00:21:32,607
Ryotsu sure is getting the short straw.

330
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:36,611
He's only doing it for himself, so I'd say all's fair.

331
00:21:39,781 --> 00:21:40,648
Croc-Vita Z!

332
00:21:41,316 --> 00:21:44,152
Clever Croc's been on TV a lot lately.

333
00:21:44,652 --> 00:21:49,691
If he's on it too much, people are likely to start getting sick of him.

334
00:21:51,125 --> 00:21:54,229
Would you like an alligator for your show?

335
00:21:55,396 --> 00:21:59,868
Oh, you've already got someone? Isn't there anything you can—

336
00:22:00,101 --> 00:22:04,606
They hung up. Damn, that's another rejection.

337
00:22:04,806 --> 00:22:05,773
Got it!

338
00:22:06,541 --> 00:22:07,976
Yes, that's right.

339
00:22:08,176 --> 00:22:09,877
You're canceling Clever Croc?

340
00:22:10,111 --> 00:22:13,681
You're tired of him? Please don't say that.

341
00:22:14,415 --> 00:22:16,684
Look. Your schedule is completely blank.

342
00:22:17,318 --> 00:22:19,687
You've got no work coming up.

343
00:22:20,355 --> 00:22:22,690
I don't need no "Croc" without the "Clever."

344
00:22:23,291 --> 00:22:26,728
I quit being your manager.

345
00:22:26,961 --> 00:22:27,662
Goodbye.

346
00:22:34,469 --> 00:22:37,739
The world is sick of your act.

347
00:22:37,972 --> 00:22:39,807
Go sort yourself out.

348
00:22:40,375 --> 00:22:42,844
I don't want anything to do with you anymore.

349
00:22:53,821 --> 00:22:55,390
Sorry I'm late, Chief.

350
00:22:55,590 --> 00:22:56,324
Ah!

351
00:22:57,125 --> 00:22:58,926
You're so thoughtful.

352
00:23:00,828 --> 00:23:02,397
What are you doing?

353
00:23:02,597 --> 00:23:03,998
Thanks, Al.

354
00:23:04,332 --> 00:23:06,200
Chief, why is he...

355
00:23:06,467 --> 00:23:09,771
Late again. Oh, to be you, Ryotsu.

356
00:23:10,204 --> 00:23:14,676
I really appreciate all the help Al gave me this morning.

357
00:23:15,209 --> 00:23:17,245
He's a quick learner,

358
00:23:17,478 --> 00:23:21,783
and he's picked up police work in no time.

359
00:23:22,016 --> 00:23:24,185
He's far more capable than you, Ryotsu.

360
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:28,323
Damn it.

361
00:23:29,057 --> 00:23:31,893
Hey, Chief. Let me massage your shoulders.

362
00:23:32,427 --> 00:23:34,629
Al already gave me a massage.

363
00:23:35,530 --> 00:23:38,366
Such obvious brown-nosing is pathetic, Ryotsu.

364
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:42,103
Excuse me, officers. Which way to Kameari Station?

365
00:23:48,509 --> 00:23:51,913
Now that we have Al, we don't need you at all, Ryotsu.

366
00:23:54,649 --> 00:23:56,584
Please let me stay!

367
00:23:56,784 --> 00:23:59,187
Let go! We don't need you.
